codex
The Triton layer norm is substantially faster, but it narrowly fails one Cauchy case because its reduction order differs from PyTorch enough to move a small output across the tolerance boundary. I’m going to adjust the variance formula to better match PyTorch’s CUDA layer norm rather than abandoning the faster path.
