codex
The explicit sqrt path helps the Cauchy shape but hurts normal inputs badly. I’m changing that into a per-row choice inside the Triton layernorm: normal-looking rows keep the faster/closer `rsqrt`, while rows with large Cauchy outliers use reciprocal sqrt.
